  "provider_query": "PEP 703 page that proposes making the CPython GIL optional",
  "answer": "**PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython**\n\n1. **Official PEP** — [peps.python.org/pep-0703](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)  \n   Sam Gross; sponsor Łukasz Langa. Status: **Final** (historical; accepted 2023). Proposes a `--disable-gil` build so CPython can run without the GIL; ABI tag includes `t` (“free-threaded”). Points to current docs on free threading. [[1]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)\n\n2. **Canonical page (alternate URL)** — [peps.python.org/pep-0703/?featured_on=talkpython](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/?featured_on=talkpython)  \n   Same PEP text: GIL blocks concurrent Python execution; default builds keep the GIL; `--disable-gil` defines `Py_GIL_DISABLED`. [[2]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/?featured_on=talkpython)\n\n3. **Steering Council acceptance** — [discuss.python.org acceptance thread](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075) (24 Oct 2023)  \n   SC accepts PEP 703 with a gradual three-phase rollout and a rollback option; prefers the term “free-threaded.” [[3]](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075)\n\n4. **Intent-to-accept notice** — [Steering Council notice](https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474) (28 Jul 2023)  \n   Intent to accept; experimental no-GIL build (expected in 3.13), then supported-but-not-default, then possible default years later. [[4]](https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474)\n\n5. **Original discussion** — [PEP 703 Discourse thread](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)  \n   Early feedback, including the configure flag naming (`--disable-gil`). [[5]](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)\n\n6. **GitHub PR that added the PEP** — [python/peps#2955](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)  \n   Merged Jan 2023 by Łukasz Langa from Sam Gross’s branch. [[6]](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)\n\n7. **PEP 779 (phase II criteria)** — [peps.python.org/pep-0779](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)  \n   Criteria for making the free-threaded build officially supported (phase II of PEP 703); targets Python 3.14. Phase III (default) left for a later decision. [[7]](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)\n\n8. **Short explainer** — [pydevtools handbook: What is PEP 703?](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)  \n   Summary: experimental free-threaded build in 3.13, supported (not default) in 3.14 under PEP 779; separate ABI (`t` wheels); default CPython still has the GIL. [[8]](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)",
